    {
      "id": "bc25b962-fa4b-4583-862f-617d92904497",
      "name": "Sticky Note6",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -128,
        48
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 640,
        "height": 736,
        "content": "## How it works\n\nThis workflow checks whether an AI-generated answer is correct before it is shared with users, customers, or internal team members. It first receives a question and its AI-generated answer, then searches the web for real-time information to verify accuracy. The system uses AI to compare the answer with real sources and calculates a confidence score. Based on this score, each response is classified as SAFE, SUSPICIOUS, or HALLUCINATED. Depending on the risk level, different actions are triggered—safe responses continue normally, suspicious ones are sent to Slack for review, and incorrect responses trigger an urgent email alert.\n\n\n\n## Setup Steps\n\n**1.** Create a webhook to receive the question and AI-generated answer.\n**2.** Use a search API (like Serper) to fetch real-time Google results.\n**3.** Format and prepare search results for AI comparison.\n**4.** Use an AI model to validate the answer and generate a confidence score.\n**5.** Apply logic to classify risk levels (SAFE / SUSPICIOUS / HALLUCINATED).\n**6.** Route results using a switch node to different actions.\n**7.** Send alerts via Slack for suspicious cases and email for critical issues.\n**8.** Return the final result to complete the workflow."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
